W: 1. How Blithe each morn was I to see
W: My lad come over the hill
W: He skipped the burn and ran to me
W: I met him with good will
W:
W: Chorus:
W:
W: Oh, the broom, the bonnie, bonnie broom
W: Broom of the Cowdenknowes
W: Fain would I be in the North Country
W: Herding his father's ewes
W:
W: 2. We neither herded ewes nor lamb
W: While the flock near us lay
W: He gathered in the sheep at night
W: And cheered me all the day
W:
W: Chorus:
W:
W: 3. Hard fate that I should banished be
W: Gone way over hill and moor
W: Because I loved the fairest lad
W: That ever yet was born
W:
W: Chorus:
W:
W: 4. Adieu, ye Cowdenknowes, adieu
W: Farewell all pleasures there
W: To wander by his side again
W: Is all I crave or care
W:
W: Chorus:
